PS2RC License, version 1.1

Copyright (c) 2026 SandstoneDev. All rights reserved, except as granted below.

This is a source-available licence, not an open-source one. It lets you study PS2RC,
use it to recompile PS2 games you own, fork it to support other games, and share your
work, as long as everything stays free of charge, you credit the original recompiler,
and the PS2RC code in your work stays under this licence. PS2RC contains no game data,
and no game data may ever be distributed with it.

0. DEFINITIONS

   "PS2RC" is the recompiler, runtime, tools, tests and documentation in this
   repository, and any part of them.
   "A Derived Work" is any software or source tree that contains PS2RC or code derived
   from it, modified or not: for example a fork, a game pack, a port of a game made with
   PS2RC, or a program built from any of these.
   "Distribute" means to give a copy to anyone else in any way, including publishing it,
   uploading it, or offering it for download.
   "Game Data" is any material taken or produced from a game's disc or files: its program
   code, in its original form or translated, recompiled or generated from it by a tool
   or by hand (including the C source PS2RC generates from a game and any program built
   from that source), its assets (graphics, models, sound, music, video, text, scripts,
   maps) and its data tables, in any form or encoding. Facts needed to work with a game,
   such as the addresses, sizes and names of the functions a game pack hooks, or the
   checksums that identify a disc, are not Game Data under this licence; whether you may
   publish them is your responsibility (section 2(f)).
   "A Listed Disc" is a game disc, identified by its disc serial, that is listed in a
   DISTRIBUTION.md notice published by SandstoneDev in a SandstoneDev repository on
   GitHub, or on the community server named in section 2(b). A notice that SandstoneDev
   published for the same purpose under version 1.0 of this licence also counts.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   Free of charge, and as long as you follow section 2, you may:
   (a) read, study and build PS2RC, and run the result;
   (b) modify PS2RC;
   (c) use PS2RC, modified or not, to recompile a game from a copy you legally own, and
       run the result yourself;
   (d) make Derived Works, including support for games that PS2RC does not support yet;
   (e) Distribute Derived Works, as source code and as programs, provided they contain
       no Game Data (section 2(d)).

2. CONDITIONS

   (a) Free of charge. Every Derived Work must be Distributed for free. You may not sell
       it, rent it, charge for it or for access to it, or put it or any part or early
       version of it behind a paywall or subscription. You may accept voluntary
       donations only if they gate nothing: no feature, build, download, early access,
       support priority or anything else may be tied to a donation, and no donation
       may be a condition of getting or using anything.
   (b) Credit the original recompiler. The documentation of every Derived Work (its
       README or equivalent), and every page where you publish or release it, must carry
       this credit:
           Based on PS2RC by SandstoneDev
           https://github.com/SandstoneDev/PS2RC
           Community: https://discord.gg/wV8x46ZTDu
       You may not remove or hide this credit, claim that you wrote PS2RC, or suggest
       that SandstoneDev endorses your work. A credit inside the program is welcome but
       not required: the start-up credit screen PS2RC ships with may be kept, changed or
       removed.
   (c) Same licence for PS2RC's code. If you Distribute the source code of a Derived
       Work, include this LICENSE file and NOTICE.md unchanged. The parts that come from
       PS2RC, and your changes to them, stay under this licence. Your own new code (for
       example a new game pack or a new module) may be under any licence that does not
       conflict with this one.
   (d) No Game Data. A Derived Work must not contain Game Data, and you must not
       Distribute Game Data with it, alongside it, or as an add-on to it: not as files,
       disc images or patches that contain it, not embedded in source code (as arrays,
       strings or encoded blobs), and not as links to copies of it. Every user supplies a
       game from a copy they legally own; translating and building a game happens on the
       user's own machine, for the user's own use.
   (e) Distribution of work for Listed Discs. You may not Distribute PS2RC, a program
       built with it, or any Derived Work that runs the game on a Listed Disc in whole
       or in part, or that is made to work with the files of a Listed Disc (for example
       a game pack or a modified game pack, a patch, a build or a conversion tool for
       it), unless SandstoneDev gives you written permission. This applies to every
       Derived Work Distributed after the disc was first listed in such a notice. One
       exception: you may keep a fork of a SandstoneDev repository on GitHub, and change
       it there, only to prepare contributions (pull requests) to that repository; you
       may not publish releases or builds from such a fork. A Derived Work made for a
       disc that is not listed, or for software of your own, is not affected. Work for a
       Listed Disc is distributed only by the PS2RC project (SandstoneDev). This is not
       a claim of any right in any game. Games, their names and all rights in them
       belong to their owners. This condition only limits how works based on PS2RC's
       code may be distributed.
   (f) Your responsibility. This licence gives no rights to any game, to any trademark,
       or to third-party code beyond what that code's own licence gives. You are
       responsible for complying with the laws that apply to you, including those on
       copies of software you own.

